mation, such as street and email addresses, telephone and fax numbers, and Web page URLs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="38453">contact</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="443471">orang hubungan</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11747_234519_305369"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An email message that is sent to a Unified Messaging subscriber that indicates that someone called but did not leave a message.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="234519">missed call notification</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="305369">pemberitahuan panggilan terlepas</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11748_136786_444097"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A display setting that holds up to 256 specific color entries. Any color palette attached to a picture is by definition an 8-bit palette.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="136786">8-bit color</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="444097">warna 8 bit</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11750_530748_2199753"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A stored procedure located on one instance of SQL Server that is executed by a statement on another instance of SQL Server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="530748">remote stored procedure</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2199753">prosedur tersimpan jauh</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11751_24376_2015088"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To use a region of memory to hold data that is waiting to be transferred, especially to or from input/output (I/O) devices such as disk drives and serial ports.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="24376">buffer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2015088">penimbal</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11754_53811_2180010"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In bulk copy, one or more characters marking the end of a field or row, separating one field or row in the data file from the next.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="53811">field terminator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2180010">penamat medan</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11755_187613_1297294"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A template that makes it possible to define and encapsulate all of the data regarding a team project. Team Foundation Server uses the methodology information to automatically configure a new team project, including creating the team project Web site.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="187613">methodology template</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1297294">templat metodologi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11757_146879_444189"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The device that communicates between your software program and your printer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="146879">printer driver</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="444189">pemacu pencetak</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11758_153847_444235"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An object created with one program and embedded into a document created by another. Embedding the object, rather than simply inserting or pasting it, ensures that the object retains its original format. If you double-click the embedded object, you can edit it with the toolbars and menus from the program used to create it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="153847">embedded object</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="444235">objek terbenam</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11759_307436_408835"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The mechanism used to help a caller differentiate between users with names that match the touch-tone or speech input.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="307436">Matched Name Selection Method</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="408835">Kaedah Pemilihan Nama Sepadan</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1176_537723_1294478"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ability for languages and classes to exchange informat