sitory of information to be synchronized.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="662158">replica</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2205180">replika</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19635_662159_2174457"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of determining which operations were made by one replica without knowledge of the other, such as when two replicas make local updates to the same item.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="662159">conflict detection</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2174457">pengesanan konflik</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19638_662163_2174356"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of clock vector elements that represents updates to a replica. Any change that occurs between 0 and the tick count is contained in the vector.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="662163">clock vector</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2174356">vektor jam</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</ter