1319594"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A kind of interpolation that averages pixel information when scaling an image. When reducing the size of an image, pixels are averaged to create a single new pixel; when an image is scaled up in size, additional pixels are created by averaging pixels of the smaller image.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="688755">interpolation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1319594">interpolasi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19850_760114_1319594"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A kind of interpolation that averages pixel information when scaling an image. When reducing the size of an image, pixels are averaged to create a single new pixel; when an image is scaled up in size, additional pixels are created by averaging pixels of the smaller image.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="760114">image interpolation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1319594">interpolasi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19869_690235_2213611"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">When referring to a commercial Microsoft volume licensing agreement, any legal entity that a party owns, that owns 