e="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21342_1266979_2587530"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To work in one location (often at home) and communicate with a main office at a different location through a personal computer equipped with a modem and communications software.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1266979">telework</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2587530">kerja dari rumah</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21342_771158_2587530"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To work in one location (often at home) and communicate with a main office at a different location through a personal computer equipped with a modem and communications software.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="771158">telecommute</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2587530">kerja dari rumah</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21348_771258_3046001"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To continue movement, as with the cursor or a search operation, to the beginning or to a new starting point rather than stopping when the end of a series is reached. For example, the screen cursor might wrap around to the first column of the next line rather than stopping when it reaches the last column of the current line. Likewise, a program starting a search or replace operation in the middle of a document might be instructed to wrap around to the beginning rather than stop when it reaches the end of the document.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="771258">wrap around</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3046001">balut keliling</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2135_50719_1294533"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ability of an object to hide its internal data and methods, making only the intended parts of the object programmatically accessible.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="50719">encapsulation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1294533">pengkapsulan</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21350_771325_1096433"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Web Part that displays a browser-enabled InfoPath form.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="771325">InfoPath Form Web Part</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1096433">Bahagian Web Borang InfoPath</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21351_1119206_1521495"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A SharePoint Server service that maintains temporary state information for InfoPath Forms Services.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1119206">Microsoft SharePoint Server State Service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1521495">Microsoft SharePoint Server State Service</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21352_771336_1686442"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that updates absolute URLs in form templates associated with SharePoint Form Libraries (i.e., InfoPath XSNs) as well as Universal Data Connection files.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="771336">Form Library URL Repair Tool</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1686442">Alat Membaiki URL Pustaka Borang</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote