oing on other websites, see their friends and their updates from other services in Windows Live, or share their Windows Live activity on other websites.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1381690">service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1517395">perkhidmatan</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27556_1381691_1461602"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A service that a user has connected to Windows Live.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1381691">connected service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1461602">servis terhubung</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2756_237244_1294561"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An attempt to model the effect of many users accessing a server at the same time. Load tests do not generate actual load with actual users, but rather simulated load with virtual users.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="237244">load simulation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1294561">simulasi beban</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote 