mmaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2787_87142_2194761"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An information model published by the Metadata Coalition (MDC) and widely supported by software vendors. The OIM is a formal description of metadata constructs organized by subject area.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="87142">Open Information Model</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2194761">Model Maklumat Terbuka</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27870_1467984_2174149"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The root abstract class Adapter, which defines the handshake between the adapter and the StreamInsight server in the ENQUEUE interaction point. It provides all the required adapter services such as memory management, and exception handling.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1467984">adapter host</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2174149">hos penyesuai</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27871_1467989_2174255"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An event stream that contains all the information needed to produce events. Either the information is an already instantiated data source, or the information is sufficient for the StreamInsight server to start the data source.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1467989">bound stream</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2174255">strim terikat</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27875_1467996_2174445"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to the ability to form complex queries by using query components (objects or operators) as reusable building blocks. This is done by linking query components together or encapsulating query components within each other.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1467996">composable</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2174445">boleh digubah</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27876_1468000_2174509"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A window with a variable window size that moves along a timeline with each distinct event start time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468000">count window</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2174509">tetingkap kiraan</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27880_1468010_2177489"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Event metadata that defines the event type.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468010">event kind</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2177489">jenis peristiwa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27881_1468013_2177485"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The portion of an event that defines the temporal properties of the event and the event kind. Temporal properties include a valid start time and end time associated with the event.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468013">event header</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2177485">pengepala peristiwa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27882_1468016_2177490"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The event metadata that defines the temporal characteristics (shape) of the event.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468016">event model</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2177490">model peristiwa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27884_1468019_2177495"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The data portion of an event in which the data fields are defined as CLR (common language runtime) types. An event payload is a typed structure.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468019">event payload</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2177495">muat beban peristiwa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27886_1468023_2175488"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">One in a pair of server instances that act as role-switching partners for a mirrored database.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468023">database mirroring partner</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2175488">pasangan pencerminan pangkalan data</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27887_1468024_2184909"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An adapter that accepts incoming event streams from external sources such as databases, files, ticker feeds, network ports, manufacturing devices and so on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468024">input adapter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2184909">penyesuai input</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27888_1468025_2174173"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A core component of an animation application and the central programmatic interface for managing (creating, scheduling, and controlling) animations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468025">animation manager</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2174173">pengurus animasi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27889_1468027_2184933"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The event kind used to signify the arrival of an event into the stream. The insert event type consists of metadata that defines the valid lifetime of the event and the payload (data) fields of the event.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468027">insert event</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2184933">peristiwa serta</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27890_1468030_2185994"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The event model of an interval event.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468030">interval event model</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2185994">model peristiwa berselang</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27892_1468034_2178422"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An explicit hierarchy used as the top level of a derived hierarchy structure.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468034">explicit cap</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2178422">tukup tak tersirat</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27893_1468036_2179992"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The server used if the connection to the partner server fails.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468036">failover partner</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2179992">rakan kongsi gagal seluruh</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27894_1468037_2194768"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An adapter that receives events processed by the server, transforms the events into a format expected by the output device (a database, text file, PDA, or other device), and emits the data to that device.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468037">output adapter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2194768">penyesuai output</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27895_1468043_2197368"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The event model of a point event.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468043">point event model</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2197368">model peristiwa titik tunggal</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><