ess by which the system extracts information that is associated with an incoming email message (subject, sender address, and recipient's addresses) that link the email activity to other Microsoft Dynamics CRM records.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1479375">smart matching</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2121744">padanan pintar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="28317_1484534_2174410"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A second data center that can provide availability within hours or days.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1484534">cold standby</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2174410">tunggu sedia sejuk</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="28354_1484614_1517350"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A disk directory entry that takes the place of a directory entry for a file but is actually a reference to a file in a different directory.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1484614">symbolic link</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1517350">pautan simbolik</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="28354_1484628_1517350"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A disk directory entry that takes the place of a directory entry for a file but is actually a reference to a file in a different directory.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1484628">symlink</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1517350">pautan simbolik</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="28354_1484629_1517350"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A disk directory entry that takes the place of a directory entry for a file but is actually a reference to a file in a different directory.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1484629">soft link</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1517350">pautan simbolik</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="28358_1585472_1944850"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A connection established between on-premises and cloud email systems that not only allows users to use email from either location with the same set of credentials, but provides a richer management experience.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1585472">Exchange hybrid deployment</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1944850">penggunaan hibrid Exchange</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2839_37265_1294562"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of instructions in some computer language intended to be executed on a computer so as to perform some task. The term usually implies a self-contained entity, as opposed to a routine or a library.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="37265">computer program</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1294562">atur cara komputer</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="28403_1484849_2214194"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of events and data returned by the Database Engine.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1484849">trace</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2214194">jejak</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</