 it will only process renewal requests.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1516667">renewal only mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1641343">mod pembaharuan sahaja</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="30520_1516672_1641534"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A hexadecimal string that contains the SHA-1 hash of the certificate.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1516672">thumbprint</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1641534">cap ibu jari</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3053_253746_2747340"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A client that waits for and accepts relayed connections.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="253746">listener</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2747340">pendengar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="30553_1517506_1691629"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Server Manager and Event Viewer, the urgency of an event or error condition, system fault, failure, or action by either the system or the user. Severity can be any of four industry-standard values: Information, Warning, Error, or Critical. These values are defined in the Event Viewer Help.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1517506">severity</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1691629">keterukan</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3056_1738272_443191"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A computer that acts as a source of information or signals. The host computer provides services, such as news, mail, or data, to computers that connect to it. The term can refer to almost any kind of computer, from a centralized mainframe that is a host to its terminals, to a server that is host to its clients, to a desktop PC that is host to its devices, such as printers and scanners.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1738272">host computer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="443191">hos</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3056_1770_443191"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A computer that acts as a source of information or signals. The host computer provides services, such as news, mail, or data, to computers that connect to it. The term can refer to almost any kind of computer, from a centralized mainframe that is a host to its terminals, to a server that is host to its clients, to a desktop PC that is host to its devices, such as printers and scanners.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1770">host</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="443191">hos</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3058_71776_443705"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A pointing device used mainly but not exclusively for computer games. A joystick has a base, on which control buttons can be mounted, and a vertical stem, which the user can move in any direction to control the movement of an object on the screen.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="71776">joystick</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="443705">kayu ria</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="30589_1517629_1641148"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A process that builds one or more certificate paths. The certificate paths may or may not trace up to a self-signed or root certificate.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1517629">certificate chaining</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1641148">perantaian sijil</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="30590_1517630_1641078"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A certificate extension used by the certificate chaining engine to determine what certificate was used to sign a presented certificate. The AKI can contain the issuer name, serial number, public key information, or no information at all. By matching the information in a certificate’s AKI extension to a CA certificate’s Subject Key Identifier (SKI) extension, a certificate chain can be built.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1517630">Authority Key Identifier</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1641078">AKI</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="30590_1517630_1641114"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A certificate extension used by the certificate chaining engine to determine what certificate was used to sign a presented certificate. The AKI can contain the issuer name, serial number, public key information, or no information at all. By matching the information in a certificate’s AKI extension to a CA certificate’s Subject Key Identifier (SKI) extension, a certificate chain can be built.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1517630">Authority Key Identifier</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1641114">Pengecam Kunci Autoriti</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="30590_1517631_1641078"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A certificate extension used by the certificate chaining engine to determine what certificate was used to sign a presented certificate. The AKI can contain the issuer name, serial number, public key information, or no information at all. By matching the information in a certificate’s AKI extension to a CA certificate’s Subject Key Identifier (SKI) extension, a certificate chain can be built.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1517631">AKI</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1641078">AKI</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="30590_1517631_1641114"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A certificate extension used by the certificate chaining engine to determine what certificate was used to sign a presented certificate. The AKI can contain the issuer name, serial number, public key information, or no information at all. By matching the information in a certificate’s AKI extension to a CA certificate’s Subject Key Identifier (SKI) extension, a certificate chain can be built.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1517631">AKI</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1641114">Pengecam Kunci Autoriti</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3060_87569_443828"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In reference to one or more computers, connected to a network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="87569">online</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="443828">dalam talian</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="30603_1518183_2388646"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A service that works in a cloud computing environment.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1518183">cloud service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2388646">perkhidmatan awan</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></la