archar data types). The SELECT statement returns those rows meeting the search criteria.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="530431">full-text query</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2181198">pertanyaan teks penuh</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="37010_2106169_2171216"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An expression in some scripting language describing how a value is to be transformed in flowing from an attribute of an entry in one directory to an attribute of an entry in another.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2106169">Custom expression</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2171216">Ungkapan tersuai</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="37011_2106171_2171223"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A property of which the value for an entry in one directory can be expected to match the value of a given property of the corresponding entry in another directory.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2106171">Joining property</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2171223">Sifat bercantum</t