tion logs that includes all log records not backed up in previous log backups. Log backups are required under the full and bulk-logged recovery models and are unavailable under the simple recovery model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="169035">log backup</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2214207">sandaran log transaksi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9196_181898_2209566"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file that is handled in a way that requires much less disk space than would otherwise be needed. Sparse support allows an application to create very large files without committing disk space for those regions of the file that contain only zeros. For example, you can use sparse support to work with a 42-GB file in which you need to write data only to the first 64 KB (the rest of the file is zeroed).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="181898">sparse file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ms"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2209566">fail jarang</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BRN, MYS</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9204_494727_2767358"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A UI container that docks to a pane, can be part of a panel group, and is represented by a tab.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><ter